      "message": "Optional / performance note on the `\"17 requests in round robin\"` cliff (570k -\u003e 1,584 calls / 300 ms on Linux):\n\nWhen a `FallbackSet` is evicted from `fFallbackSets(16)` and later recreated, every coverage class match re-runs `FontAccessible(font)` on line 931 before checking `fTFCache` in `createTypefaceFromFcPattern`. Because `FontAccessible` calls `SkData::MakeFromFileName`, an LRU miss reads the entire font file (10–25 MB for CJK/emoji `.ttc`s) from disk into memory even when the `SkTypeface` is already cached in `fTFCache`.\n\nIncreasing the `fFallbackSets` capacity (e.g. to 64, since each `FallbackSet` only holds a pattern and a small `classId -\u003e sk_sp\u003cSkTypeface\u003e` map) or checking `fTFCache` before calling `FontAccessible` would avoid re-reading font files on LRU turnover.",
      "revId": "a3c538167ac78e36df668472863faef4ed2ff778",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
