      "side": 1,
      "message": "`if (page \u003e 0x10FF) { return 0; }` should be checked right after computing `page` on line 958 rather than only guarding `fCoverage.fEmptyPages.add(page)` on line 982:\n\n1. For `0x1100 \u003c\u003d page \u003c\u003d 0xFFFF`, skipping `fEmptyPages` causes every call to allocate `maps` and scan all `fCoverage.fCharSets` from scratch.\n2. For `page \u003e\u003d 0x10000` (e.g. `character \u003e\u003d 0x1000000` or negative `SkUnichar`), FontConfig\u0027s `FcCharSetFindLeafPos` truncates `ucs4 \u003e\u003e 8` to `FcChar16` (`uint16_t`). When the truncated 16-bit page exists in a font (such as `0x0000`), `FcCharSetIterSet` leaves `ai.ucs4` untouched at `page \u003c\u003c 8`, so `FcCharSetNextPage(...) \u003d\u003d page \u003c\u003c 8` evaluates to `true` and populates `fCoverage.fPageClasses` with unbounded out-of-Unicode keys.",
      "revId": "a3c538167ac78e36df668472863faef4ed2ff778",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
