      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. Your analysis is correct. In fontconfig 2.18.3, FcCharSetFindLeafForward takes the page as FcChar16. When the leaf exists, FcCharSetIterSet keeps iter-\u003eucs4, so FcCharSetNextPage returns page \u003c\u003c 8. With PS1, 65536 calls with pages 0x10000 to 0x1FFFF added about 11 MB to RSS. U+110000 again and again scanned all charsets in each call: 33115 calls per 300 ms.\n\nNow coverageClass returns class 0 (nullptr) immediately after it calculates the page, if page \u003e 0x10FF. The bound check on fEmptyPages is removed. The same 65536 calls add 64 KB (the code before this change: 72 KB), and U+110000 gives 1100294 calls per 300 ms.\n\nAbout the result of the code before this change: for -1, 0x110000, 0x1000000, 0xFFFFFF and 0x7FFFFFFF, it returns nullptr, the same as now. But FcCharSetHasChar in FontContainsCharacter has the same 16-bit truncation. Thus for 0x1000041, 0x80000041 and 0xFF000041, that code returns the font of \u0027A\u0027 (Noto Sans for \"en\"). PS1 also returned fonts for these characters. Now all characters out of Unicode return nullptr. Unicode has no character above U+10FFFF, so the result is nullptr. The new test checks -1, 0x110000 and 0x1000000 (the same result as before) and 0x1000041 (nullptr; before this change and with PS1, Roboto).",
